<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-flask" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Flask Framework</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> The "back-end" of a web application has a number of 
      routine tasks to do, regardless of the programming language (Python,
      JavaScript, Perl, etc) and so libraries/modules and other software
      infrastructure have been created to make this routine work easier.
      <strong>Flask</strong> is one such framework. There are others,
    such as Django and Pyramid. We'll cover Flask.</p>
  </introduction>

